# The granted flashback changes the cost and the zone, not the timing (CR 702.34a, 117.1a). Bot1 casts Chain Lightning (a
# sorcery) at Bot2, then Stingcaster Mage with Black Lotus's red mana. While the Mage's trigger is on the stack the Chain
# Lightning in the graveyard is not offered (a sorcery needs an empty stack); once the trigger has resolved, in the main
# phase, it is, for {R} (its mana cost) out of what the Lotus left, and it is exiled afterwards. Bot2 takes 3 + 3.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Black Lotus
Chain Lightning
Stingcaster Mage
Forest x3
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chain Lightning.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Stingcaster Mage.Cast
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 1
! Bot1.Graveyard.Chain Lightning.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Graveyard.Chain Lightning.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 14
Exile = Chain Lightning
Bot1.Graveyard = Black Lotus
